# Deploy to GitHub on Every Change

When the user requests code changes in this project, **always commit and push to GitHub** in the same session — do not leave changes local-only.

## Workflow (after completing edits)

1. Run `node --check app.js` if `app.js` changed.
2. Run `node scripts/sync-www.js` to sync the `www/` folder (Capacitor + GitHub Pages).
3. Bump `sw.js` cache version (`family-hub-vN`) when static assets change.
4. `git add` changed files, commit with a concise message, `git push origin HEAD`.

## Notes

- GitHub Pages serves from the repo root: https://yujsid.github.io/family-hub/
- The user expects live site updates without a separate deploy step.
- Only skip push if the user explicitly says not to, or if there are no file changes.
